Error: Jet.HiddenCopyInLoop: An exact Int operation may spill to bigint inside a loop
  --> Tests/UI/cost_spill_doubling_in_loop.jet:6:23
    |
  6 |     loop _ in rows -> span *= 2
    |                       ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The loop multiplies or shifts this Int on every turn and nothing caps it, so it outgrows the packed Int rail and goes on as a bigint.
 Fix: To keep the Int on the packed rail, give it a range type such as `Int(0..1000)` or a fixed width such as `I64`, or cap it in the loop's condition.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.HiddenCopyInLoop
